{% comment %}
  SBS - central US market product eligibility rule.

  Single source of truth for (a) which products are APPROVED for sale in the
  US market and (b) which of those approved products are currently
  DISCOVERY-ENABLED, meaning they may appear in US storefront discovery
  surfaces such as collection cards, search result cards, predictive search,
  recommendation cards, mega-menu tiles, top-searched pills, product
  scrollers, the quote-modal product picker and cart recommendations.

  Release: US Catalogue Expansion - Omni & Anja.

  Two distinct sets
  -----------------
  APPROVED           may be sold in the US and must render correctly when a
                     shopper reaches the product directly by URL.
  DISCOVERY-ENABLED  a subset of APPROVED. Only these products may be
                     surfaced by US discovery surfaces. A product is added
                     here only after it has passed direct-URL canary QA.

  Usage
  -----
    Discovery surfaces (default scope):

      {%- capture sbs_us_eligibility -%}
        {%- render 'sbs-us-eligibility', product: product -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- unless sbs_us_eligibility contains 'DENY' -%}
        ... render the card ...
      {%- endunless -%}

    Product-level rendering that must work for any approved model reached by
    direct URL, for example US pricing, 120V and UL Listed copy:

      {%- render 'sbs-us-eligibility', product: product, scope: 'approved' -%}

  Accepted inputs, any one is enough:
    product  a Shopify product object
    handle   a product handle string
    url      a product URL string containing /products/<handle>

  Optional inputs:
    scope    'approved' to test the approved set. Anything else, including
             blank, tests the discovery-enabled set.

  List mode, for client-side renderers that must share the same source of
  truth:
    list: 'allowed_handles'   discovery-enabled handles
    list: 'allowed_ids'       discovery-enabled product IDs
    list: 'enabled_handles'   discovery-enabled handles
    list: 'enabled_ids'       discovery-enabled product IDs
    list: 'approved_handles'  approved handles
    list: 'approved_ids'      approved product IDs

  Output is exactly one token:
    ALLOW  render normally
    DENY   do not render for this US session

  Behaviour:
    * Non-US sessions always receive ALLOW. Other markets are never affected.
    * Neutral input with no resolvable product receives ALLOW so that pages,
      collections, articles, policies and general content are never hidden.
    * Products are matched on stable numeric product IDs first and on exact
      handles only when no ID is available. No title substring matching.
    * Any resolvable product outside the tested set receives DENY.

  US APPROVED products - Folio family:
    7836616818913  office-phone-booth-soundproof-folio-private-workspace
    7976286322913  office-phone-booth-stand-up-soundproof-meeting-pod
    8159685771489  folio-office-pod-2-4-person-soundproof-meeting-booth

  US APPROVED products - Omni family (template suffix omni-booth):
    9532084289761  omni-one
    9532084388065  omni-one-plus
    9532084519137  omni-two
    9532084617441  omni-demi
    9532084650209  omni-four
    9532084715745  omni-six
    9532084814049  omni-sleep-pod

  US APPROVED products - Anja family:
    9539197698273  anja-m
    9551092187361  anja-s

  Products whose title merely contains Folio or Omni (Folio 4-Person Sofa,
  Folio Solo Booth Sofa, Omni Corner Sofa, Omni Demi Sofa, Omni Four Sofa,
  Omni One Plus Sofa, Omni Sleep Pod Bed, Omni Flow, Omni Group and the Omni
  Module range) are standalone furniture and accessory products, not booth
  models, and are deliberately NOT approved.

  To add a product to the US market, add its numeric ID and exact handle to
  the approved lists below and add it to the US market catalog in Shopify.
  To make an approved product discoverable, add it to the enabled lists below
  in the final activation commit.

  Scopes
  ------
    (default)          discovery-enabled subset - use for every US discovery
                       surface (cards, search, menus, recommendations).
    'approved'         full approved set - use for direct-URL correctness such
                       as US copy adaptation, pricing and schema.
    'compliance_block' approved Omni and Anja only - drives the shared US
                       compliance component snippets/us-compliance-block.liquid.
    'iso_23351'        approved products whose existing content already
                       supports ISO 23351-1 and may therefore display it.

  List modes (return the raw comma-delimited set instead of a verdict):
    'enabled_ids' / 'enabled_handles' / 'allowed_ids' / 'allowed_handles'
    'approved_ids' / 'approved_handles'
    'compliance_ids' / 'compliance_handles'
    'iso_ids' / 'iso_handles'

{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign sbs_elig_approved_ids = ',7836616818913,7976286322913,8159685771489,9532084289761,9532084388065,9532084519137,9532084617441,9532084650209,9532084715745,9532084814049,9539197698273,9551092187361,'
  assign sbs_elig_approved_handles = ',office-phone-booth-soundproof-folio-private-workspace,office-phone-booth-stand-up-soundproof-meeting-pod,folio-office-pod-2-4-person-soundproof-meeting-booth,omni-one,omni-one-plus,omni-two,omni-demi,omni-four,omni-six,omni-sleep-pod,anja-m,anja-s,'

  # Discovery-enabled subset. Extended only by the final activation commit,
  # after each model has passed direct-URL canary QA.
  assign sbs_elig_enabled_ids = ',7836616818913,7976286322913,8159685771489,'
  assign sbs_elig_enabled_handles = ',office-phone-booth-soundproof-folio-private-workspace,office-phone-booth-stand-up-soundproof-meeting-pod,folio-office-pod-2-4-person-soundproof-meeting-booth,'


  # Compliance-block set. Approved Omni and Anja models render the shared US
  # compliance component snippets/us-compliance-block.liquid. The three Folio
  # models are deliberately excluded: their existing tick list already states
  # 120V, UL Listed and ISO 23351-1 for the US market through
  # snippets/us-product-copy.liquid, so adding the block to Folio would
  # duplicate an equivalent compliant section.
  assign sbs_elig_compliance_ids = ',9532084289761,9532084388065,9532084519137,9532084617441,9532084650209,9532084715745,9532084814049,9539197698273,9551092187361,'
  assign sbs_elig_compliance_handles = ',omni-one,omni-one-plus,omni-two,omni-demi,omni-four,omni-six,omni-sleep-pod,anja-m,anja-s,'

  # ISO 23351-1 support set. Only products whose existing product content
  # already supports the standard may display it. Evidence:
  #   Folio  tick list 'Acoustic ISO-2355-1 Accredited' plus the 2-4 person
  #          FAQ answers that reference ISO 23351-1.
  #   Omni   custom.finer_details 'Sound/Acoustics' -> 'ISO 23351-1 Grade A+'.
  # Anja product content contains no ISO statement, so Anja is excluded and
  # must never display an ISO claim.
  assign sbs_elig_iso_ids = ',7836616818913,7976286322913,8159685771489,9532084289761,9532084388065,9532084519137,9532084617441,9532084650209,9532084715745,9532084814049,'
  assign sbs_elig_iso_handles = ',office-phone-booth-soundproof-folio-private-workspace,office-phone-booth-stand-up-soundproof-meeting-pod,folio-office-pod-2-4-person-soundproof-meeting-booth,omni-one,omni-one-plus,omni-two,omni-demi,omni-four,omni-six,omni-sleep-pod,'

  assign sbs_elig_test_ids = sbs_elig_enabled_ids
  assign sbs_elig_test_handles = sbs_elig_enabled_handles
  if scope == 'approved'
    assign sbs_elig_test_ids = sbs_elig_approved_ids
    assign sbs_elig_test_handles = sbs_elig_approved_handles
  elsif scope == 'compliance_block'
    assign sbs_elig_test_ids = sbs_elig_compliance_ids
    assign sbs_elig_test_handles = sbs_elig_compliance_handles
  elsif scope == 'iso_23351'
    assign sbs_elig_test_ids = sbs_elig_iso_ids
    assign sbs_elig_test_handles = sbs_elig_iso_handles
  endif

  assign sbs_elig_verdict = 'ALLOW'

  if list == 'allowed_handles' or list == 'enabled_handles'
    assign sbs_elig_verdict = sbs_elig_enabled_handles
  elsif list == 'allowed_ids' or list == 'enabled_ids'
    assign sbs_elig_verdict = sbs_elig_enabled_ids
  elsif list == 'approved_handles'
    assign sbs_elig_verdict = sbs_elig_approved_handles
  elsif list == 'approved_ids'
    assign sbs_elig_verdict = sbs_elig_approved_ids
  elsif list == 'compliance_handles'
    assign sbs_elig_verdict = sbs_elig_compliance_handles
  elsif list == 'compliance_ids'
    assign sbs_elig_verdict = sbs_elig_compliance_ids
  elsif list == 'iso_handles'
    assign sbs_elig_verdict = sbs_elig_iso_handles
  elsif list == 'iso_ids'
    assign sbs_elig_verdict = sbs_elig_iso_ids
  elsif localization.country.iso_code == 'US'
    assign sbs_elig_id = ''
    assign sbs_elig_handle = ''

    if product != blank
      assign sbs_elig_id = product.id | append: ''
      assign sbs_elig_handle = product.handle
    endif

    if sbs_elig_handle == blank and handle != blank
      assign sbs_elig_handle = handle
    endif

    if sbs_elig_handle == blank and url != blank
      if url contains '/products/'
        assign sbs_elig_handle = url | split: '/products/' | last | split: '?' | first | split: '#' | first
      endif
    endif

    assign sbs_elig_id_key = ',' | append: sbs_elig_id | append: ','
    assign sbs_elig_handle_key = ',' | append: sbs_elig_handle | append: ','

    if sbs_elig_id != blank
      if sbs_elig_test_ids contains sbs_elig_id_key
        assign sbs_elig_verdict = 'ALLOW'
      else
        assign sbs_elig_verdict = 'DENY'
      endif
    elsif sbs_elig_handle != blank
      if sbs_elig_test_handles contains sbs_elig_handle_key
        assign sbs_elig_verdict = 'ALLOW'
      else
        assign sbs_elig_verdict = 'DENY'
      endif
    else
      assign sbs_elig_verdict = 'ALLOW'
    endif
  endif
-%}
{{- sbs_elig_verdict -}}
